---
import { HERO } from '../content/home'
---

<section class="relative flex min-h-[620px] flex-col items-center justify-end overflow-hidden lg:h-195">
    {/* The photograph is an <img> rather than a background so it can be
        preloaded with fetchpriority and decoded eagerly — it is the LCP. */}
    <img
        src={HERO.image}
        srcset={HERO.imageSrcset}
        sizes={HERO.imageSizes}
        alt={HERO.imageAlt}
        class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
        fetchpriority="high"
        decoding="async"
    />

    {/* Scrim: pared back to the least that keeps white type legible, so the
        photograph carries the frame. It is all but clear across the canopy and
        only gathers weight where the copy sits. Every stop was solved against
        the photograph's own pixels — the lowest alpha per 20px slice that
        clears AA on the single worst pixel under the column — then rounded up.

        Re-measured for the firepit photograph, whose flames blow out to pure
        white (255,255,255) under the left of the copy column at every desktop
        width. On that worst pixel, white reads:
            headline  62px        4.51:1  ✅ AA  (needs 3:1, large text)
            sub-head  22px italic 5.33:1  ✅ AA  (needs 4.5:1 — at this size it
                                                  is not large text)
        The 70% stop went 0.64 → 0.66 for the sub-head, whose top edge cleared
        4.5:1 by 0.006 alpha before that — passing by rounding rather than by
        margin. It is the stop with no room left in it.

        The 44% stop has headroom now: the one-line headline starts at 61% of
        the frame rather than 44%, where the gradient has already reached 0.61.
        It is held at 0.52 for the case where the headline does wrap after all
        — a viewport near 1024px, or Georgia rendering before Cormorant loads —
        which puts its first line back at 44% and still clears AA, at 3.40:1.

        A new photograph means this measured again. At phone widths object-cover
        crops the fire out of frame, so the wide viewports are the worst case. */}
    <div
        class="absolute inset-0"
        style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(35,32,27,0.02) 0%, rgba(35,32,27,0.52) 44%, rgba(35,32,27,0.66) 70%, rgba(35,32,27,0.7) 100%)"
        aria-hidden="true"
    >
    </div>

    {/* One centred stack on the floor of the frame: the headline, the italic
        line, then the single call to action.

        The column widens to max-w-270 at lg so the headline sets on one line.
        It is 886px at 62px/500 with the -0.01em tracking, and the tightest lg
        viewport — 1024px, where max-w-270 is not yet reached — leaves 920px
        inside the 52px gutters. Two lines at 72px cost more than the 10px of
        type: the second line pushed the stack up over the fire. The sub-head
        keeps its own max-w-215, so its measure is unchanged.

        Less bottom padding at lg than below it, which reads backwards but is
        not: the section is 780px tall there against a 620px minimum, and the
        stack is pushed down into that extra height to get out of the couple's
        way. At 48px its top edge sits at 478px, and the table they are sitting
        at ends at 458px — so both faces, the table and the glasses stay in the
        open above the headline. Raising this back up covers them. */}
    <div class="gutter relative flex w-full max-w-240 flex-col items-center gap-6 pt-32 pb-16 lg:max-w-270 lg:gap-7 lg:pb-12">
        <h1
            class="font-display max-w-215 text-center text-[40px] leading-[1.08] font-medium tracking-[-0.01em] text-balance text-white sm:text-[54px] lg:max-w-none lg:text-[62px] lg:leading-[1.06]"
        >
            {HERO.heading}
        </h1>
        <p
            class="font-display max-w-215 text-center text-[18px] leading-7.5 text-balance text-white italic sm:text-[20px] sm:leading-8 lg:text-[22px] lg:leading-9"
        >
            {HERO.subheading}
        </p>
        <a
            href={HERO.cta.href}
            class="mt-2 flex items-center justify-center bg-primary px-9 py-4.75 text-center text-[12px] leading-4 font-medium tracking-[0.18em] text-white uppercase transition-colors hover:bg-[#083329]"
        >
            {HERO.cta.label}
        </a>
    </div>
</section>
